{% import 'dashboard/_macros.html.twig' as ui %}
<div class="scroll"><table class="dense"><tbody>
{% for k, label in {total: 'Total recipients', waiting: 'Waiting (job not started — e.g. HELD mode)', queued: 'Queued in the delivery daemon', submitted: 'Submitted to Postfix', remote_accepted: 'Remote accepted', deferred: 'Deferred (retrying)', soft_bounced: 'Soft bounced', hard_bounced: 'Hard bounced', complaints: 'Complaints', suppressed: 'Suppressed (not sent)', failed: 'Failed', outcome_unknown: 'Outcome unknown', unresolved: 'Still unresolved', open_observed: 'Open observed', clicked: 'Clicked'} %}
<tr><th scope="row">{{ label }}</th><td class="num">{{ (attribute(report, k) ?? 0)|number_format }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="caveat">“Remote accepted” means the recipient's mail server took responsibility for the message. It does not prove inbox placement (it may be in spam) or that anyone read it.
“Open observed” means the tracking image was fetched — by the person, their mail client, a privacy proxy or a security scanner; many real readers never load images. {{ ui.help('delivery-states', 'What these mean') }}</p>
